Model attribution

The Apple Silicon runtime uses mlx-community/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-4bit,
a quantized conversion of Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507. Both model cards
identify their license as Apache 2.0. Model weights are downloaded separately
and are not included in this repository.

https://huggingface.co/mlx-community/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-4bit
https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507

The optional Ollama runtime uses qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M.
It is a separate quantization and its results may differ from the MLX recordings.

https://ollama.com/library/qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M

Football data

The local Premier League 2024-25 export comes from the existing ONTHEDOT
database, originally populated through API-Football. The public catalog contains
names, aliases, scope and a dataset fingerprint. The full provider dataset stays
in the ignored .local directory. Publication rights for that data have not been
established. The provider terms do not grant a publication license.

https://www.api-football.com/terms

No production database, credentials, account information or provider responses
are included. Small synthetic records are used only in automated tests.
